  "representation_invariants": [
    "LinearVectorGrowth consumes the original vector. It implements no Deref, Index, slice, iterator or AsRef. Checked extraction returns the still-owning token while original slots are dead.",
    "Before original destruction begins, the allocation is converted without moving elements into ManuallyDrop<Vec<MaybeUninit<T>>>. The interrupted state never owns a partially dead Vec<T>. The fully constructed replacement remains a separate ManuallyDrop owner.",
    "Original destruction increments dead_end before drop_in_place, so the throwing slot is dead too. Reconstruction writes only [restored,dead_end), incrementing restored after a returned value is successfully placed. Every repair-panic boundary preserves exact remaining holes.",
    "Only metadata and raw addresses are observable during interruption. No safe reference can span a dead slot. Unsafe entry explicitly forbids aliasing live original-slot/owned-payload references or callback receiver aliases.",
    "Successful old-range destruction frees its MaybeUninit backing allocation without another T destructor, then publishes the complete replacement. Full reconstruction reconstitutes Vec<T> from the identical allocation and permits extraction.",
    "Dropping an interrupted token intentionally leaks both allocations rather than reading/dropping invalid values. This is a sound Rust containment fallback with no native parity credit for dropping an unrepaired invalid native object. Production repair never implicitly destroys/frees the abandoned replacement.",
    "Only cfg(test) accessors extract abandoned replacement ownership and original raw storage for typed cleanup after native observations. They are absent from production rustdoc. No allocator ownership helper or global registry is introduced."
  ],
